tasks.description:
`src/lib/timeline.ts`, matching the legacy timeline code in `renderStats`:
- completion events from done tasks' timestamps;
- bucket count **clamped to 4–16**, and bucket assignment;
- min/max range and date formatting.

Unit tests, including no timestamps, a single completion and identical timestamps.

`src/lib/graph/layout.ts`, matching legacy `renderDepGraph`:
- **topological layering** of the filtered tasks (only visible deps count; a cycle dumps the remaining tasks into one layer);
- node positions: `nodeW 160`, `nodeH 52`, `padX 60`, `padY 24`, layers vertically centered;
- an edge list with bezier path data;
- total width/height, and `truncate(name, 22)`.

Unit tests: chain, diamond, cycle, hidden deps, empty input.

Add `src/lib/prefs.ts`: typed get/set helpers for per-browser dashboard preferences, stored in `localStorage` under **one namespaced key** (e.g. `"atm-dashboard"`).

Every read/write is wrapped in `try`/`catch`: when storage is unavailable or the stored value is corrupt, reads return the given default and writes are no-ops (**no exceptions, no console errors**).

Unit tests (jsdom):
- round trip;
- defaults when empty;
- corrupt JSON;
- a `localStorage` whose methods throw.

See `docs/dashboard-v2-requirements.md` FR-6.2.

Make auto-refresh **default to ON (5 s)** and persist the on/off choice and interval via `src/lib/prefs.ts` (FR-6.1, FR-6.2).

### Test isolation first
`openDashboard()` in `tests/e2e/helpers.ts` must store auto-refresh **OFF** via `page.addInitScript` before navigation, unless called with `{ autoRefresh: true }`, so existing specs (request counts, screenshots) are unaffected by background reloads.

### Specs
Replace the refresh.spec test *is off by default* with:
- on by default (fresh browser, no init script);
- polls every 5 s (`page.clock`);
- switching off survives a page reload;
- a changed interval survives a reload.

Update the state unit tests. **Screenshots must not change** (the visual spec runs with auto-refresh off).

### Behaviour
Change `DepGraph` so **only the first successful layout auto-fits**. Afterwards, when the visible task set changes (filters or a reload):
- **always keep `k`** (whether or not the user zoomed);
- keep the pan if `anyNodeVisible()`, otherwise `panToContent()` with the in-progress/next-todo focus (FR-6.3, FR-6.4).

The minimap and zoom label follow (FR-6.5). Window resize/expand behaviour stays as today.

### Specs
Replace the graph-zoom spec *changing the visible tasks re-fits* with:
- zoom in, filter by a phase → the zoom label is unchanged;
- a filter whose nodes would all be off-screen → the view pans (same `k`) and at least one node is in the viewport;
- clearing the filter keeps `k`;
- the fit button still fits.

Update `/atm:do-task` and `/atm:loop-tasks`:
- when setting `in_progress`, also set `started_at`;
- when setting `done`, also set `completed_at`;
- when a task fails and goes back to `todo`, remove `started_at` / `completed_at`;
- always keep updating `updated_at`.

Use the same `date -u` command the skills already use, and keep the wording consistent between the two skills.

Verify by **reading both files end to end** (no automated test covers skill text); `npm run verify` must still pass.

Add `src/lib/changelog.ts`:
- **`parseChangelog(markdown)`** → `[{ version, date, sections: [{ title, items[] }] }]` (newest first; supports `[Unreleased]`);
- **`compareVersions(a, b)`** for `x.y.z`;
- **`entriesBetween(entries, fromExclusive, toInclusive)`**, treating a missing version as `0.0.0`.

Pure TS, **no Markdown library**; inline Markdown in items is kept as plain text.

Unit tests against the real `plugin/CHANGELOG.md`, plus edge cases (empty file, missing date, unknown section names).

### Changelog
Turn `[Unreleased]` into `[0.7.0] - <date>`:
- auto-refresh on by default;
- the graph keeps its zoom on filter changes;
- the What's new panel;
- `/atm:update-dashboard` shows real release notes;
- `started_at` / `completed_at`.

### Release
- Bump `plugin.json` and `marketplace.json` to **0.7.0**, and rebuild.
- Update the README (dashboard features; the *Auto refresh* tip in Quick Start is no longer needed).
- Copy the build to `docs/tasks-dashboard.html`.
- `npm run verify` green.

Add `tests/fixtures/kanban.json` with:
- every status, including an unknown one;
- todo tasks that are ready and waiting (including waiting on a missing id);
- several `in_progress` tasks with `started_at`;
- more than 20 done tasks with distinct `completed_at`;
- skipped tasks;
- 3 phases.

The fixtures smoke spec must load it **without errors**.

### e2e `kanban.spec`
On `kanban.json` and `standard`:
- columns and counts;
- card order per column;
- readiness text;
- *Next up* on the right card (and it moves after a reload where that task is done);
- the detail panel opens on click;
- the skipped toggle and *Show all*;
- a status filter limits the columns;
- live update via Reload.

### Screenshots
Add Kanban screenshots to `visual.spec` (`standard`, `kanban`): darwin baselines; CI generates linux.

Add `tests/fixtures/progress.json` with:
- 3 phases across several days;
- done tasks with `started_at` / `completed_at` (and some with only `updated_at`);
- an idle gap of hours between sessions;
- tasks added midway (later `created_at`);
- one blocked and one skipped task;
- phase 0 fully done.

**Document the intended expected numbers** (pace, ranges, ETAs at a fixed *now*) in a comment block in the generator or a sibling README, so tests can cite them.

`src/lib/burndown.ts`:
- step series of **remaining tasks** and of **total scope** over time (by `created_at`; the done time from `completed_at` / `updated_at`);
- a **forecast segment** from now to the projected finish (from `forecast.ts`);
- an optional phase filter for FR-4.6;
- handles a missing `created_at` (falls back to the earliest known timestamp).

Unit tests.

The **phase table** in the Progress tab.

### Columns and content
- the phase (in its phase colour), done/total, a progress bar, remaining;
- the state: *Done* / *In progress* / *Not started*;
- the estimate: *"≈ 1 h 10 m of agent work (50 m - 1 h 40 m)"*, with the calendar time secondary (*"if the loop keeps running: ..."*);
- the done date for finished phases;
- a blocked warning;
- *"based on the last N tasks: ~X min each"*;
- *"Not enough history to estimate"* when applicable.

### Tests
e2e with `page.clock` at a fixed time, on `progress.json` and on a fixture with too little history.
